flowchart TB
  accTitle: What a workflow of a repository calls
  accDescr: A workflow of the repository, such as issue-assistant.yml, holds what starts it, the most permissions that its jobs get, and one pin, of a release of the issue assistant. It calls the reusable workflow of that release, whose jobs run in the repository, with its events, variables, environment issue-assistant and firewall policy, and each job runs the issue assistant of the same commit. A new release reaches the repository as a pull request of Dependabot or Renovate that moves the pin; install runs again only when a release changes a template.
  subgraph repository ["your repository"]
    direction TB
    caller["`**.github/workflows/issue-assistant.yml**<br>what starts it, the most permissions,<br>one pin of a release`"]
    own(["its events, variables,<br>environment issue-assistant<br>and firewall policy"])
  end
  subgraph release ["Dennis-Otto/issue-assistant at the pinned commit"]
    direction TB
    jobs["`**reusable-issue-assistant.yml**<br>the jobs event, analyze and apply`"]
    tool["the issue assistant<br>of the same commit"]
  end
  update(["a new release:<br>Dependabot or Renovate<br>moves the pin"])
  update --> caller
  caller -- "calls at the commit" --> jobs
  own -. "the jobs run with them" .-> jobs
  jobs -- "each job runs" --> tool
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef release fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
  class caller,own job
  class jobs,tool release
  class update trigger
